  "date": "2022-02",
  "title": "Exhibition And Events On The Un Sustainable Development Goals",
  "language": "en",
  "paragraphs": [
    {
      "heading": "Exhibition and events",
      "text": "What contribution can science and technology make to fighting global poverty, protecting the planet, and ensuring that by 2030 all people enjoy peace and prosperity?\n\nIn 2015, the 193 UN members have adopted the 2030 Agenda for sustainable development. At the heart of this global action plan for promoting human well-being and protecting the environment are the 17 Sustainable Development Goals (SDGs). As research institutions and training grounds for future leaders of sustainable development, universities play a key role in achieving the SDGs."
    },
    {
      "heading": "Exhibition and events",
      "text": "For the second time, the exhibition and event programme \"Together for the SDGs\" is taking place at ETH Zurich to raise awareness and inspire action for the Sustainable Development Goals. In the exhibition at ETH Campus Hönggerberg, visitors can engage with the SDGs through art and learn about examples of research and education at ETH Zurich that contribute to the SDGs. In addition to a guided tour of the exhibition, a pitch and a storytelling event at the Student Project House offer the opportunity to exchange ideas with students committed to global sustainable development."
    },
    {
      "heading": "Together for the SDGs Agenda",
      "text": "7 – 18 March 2022 ETH Hönggerberg, HPH Building, D-Hall Monday-​Friday: 7:30-20:30\n\nTuesday, 8 March 2022 16:00-18:00 Student Project House Clausiusstrasse 16\n\nThursday, 10 March 2022 17:15-​19:30 Student Project House, Clausiusstrasse 16\n\nFriday, 11 March 2022 17:30-​19:00 ETH Hönggerberg, HPH Building, D-​Hall"
    }
  ],
